\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.1}{\ignorespaces Comparison of no drift versus drift scenarios. Left: When distributions overlap, the adversarial classifier cannot distinguish data sources (AUC $\approx $ 0.5). Right: When drift occurs, distributions shift and the classifier can distinguish sources (AUC $>>$ 0.5).}}{5}{figure.caption.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.1}{\ignorespaces Overview of Explainable Adversarial Drift Detection (EADD) methodology. Blue boxes indicate novel contributions: Permutation Test (Step 3) and SHAP Feature Attribution (Step 4). The framework extends D3's adversarial validation with statistical rigor and root cause analysis.}}{20}{figure.caption.3}%
